Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.89,0:00:29.81,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.41,0:00:31.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Y 'all move!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.95,0:01:02.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry up!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.86,0:01:04.02,Default,,0,0,0,,The duel's about to start!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.11,0:01:06.88,Default,,0,0,0,,It's being broadcast live\Nall around the world!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.75,0:01:09.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember our deal, Devlin.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.39,0:01:11.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I win this and you let Joey go.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.61,0:01:13.61,Default,,0,0,0,,No more dog suit, no more demands.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.23,0:01:15.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Agreed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.14,0:01:17.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Just don't forget the\Nflip side to that coin.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.77,0:01:22.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You lose this game, and you promise to\Nnever play Duel Monsters ever again.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.75,0:01:24.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Now!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.66,0:01:25.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's get it on!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.55,0:01:31.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks a bit different\Nthan a dueling arena, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.87,0:01:33.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, get used to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.29,0:01:37.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Dungeon Dice Monsters is a whole new\Ngame with a whole new set of rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.29,0:01:40.82,Default,,0,0,0,,And to keep up, you're going\Nto have to pay close attention.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.71,0:01:42.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.89,0:01:44.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm a quick study.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.49,0:01:47.95,Default,,0,0,0,,You better be, Yugi, because I\Nknow this game inside and out.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.03,0:01:50.97,Default,,0,0,0,,And if you want to win, you're\Ngoing to have to learn it as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.05,0:01:52.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Now let's get started.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.03,0:01:56.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks pretty straightforward
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.09,0:02:00.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Lost already? Relax,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.03,0:02:05.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll walk you through it. That's\Nyour dice pool. Select 15 dice from
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.19,0:02:09.11,Default,,0,0,0,,it to use for the game I'd give\Nyou some tips on which to pick,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.27,0:02:13.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi But being the master gamer that\Nyou are, I'm sure you'll figure it out
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.47,0:02:19.35,Default,,0,0,0,,With all these different colors and designs,\Nit's hard to know which ones to choose
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.51,0:02:23.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry up now I got mine already set.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.51,0:02:25.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm ready too. Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.53,0:02:26.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Now here's how it works.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.01,0:02:29.91,Default,,0,0,0,,These dice are gonna be\Nkinda like your dueling deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.99,0:02:33.85,Default,,0,0,0,,And just like you shuffle your\Ndeck, we shuffle these. Like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.65,0:02:37.77,Default,,0,0,0,,See? Easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.13,0:02:42.11,Default,,0,0,0,,The Dice Automator will randomize\Nyour 15 dice in groups of three.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.51,0:02:43.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Take a look.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.81,0:02:45.67,Default,,0,0,0,,You get three dice per round.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.89,0:02:47.69,Default,,0,0,0,,You roll all three at the same time,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.77,0:02:50.57,Default,,0,0,0,,and then you get to make your\Nmove depending on what you roll.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.65,0:02:53.30,Default,,0,0,0,,But I'll explain more\Nabout that a bit later.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.21,0:02:56.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, take the three die\Nout of the auto hatch.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.15,0:02:59.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.06,0:03:01.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, how do you score?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.57,0:03:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, in this game, we have heart points.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.33,0:03:06.85,Default,,0,0,0,,They're like life points,\Nonly you only get three.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.93,0:03:07.76,Default,,0,0,0,,That's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.84,0:03:10.96,Default,,0,0,0,,And whoever loses all three\Nof their hearts first is out.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.25,0:03:12.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Game on!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.87,0:03:13.97,Default,,0,0,0,,What game on?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.11,0:03:15.83,Default,,0,0,0,,But Yuki just now learned the rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.91,0:03:18.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's probably\Njust how Duke likes it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.29,0:03:20.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Go! Go! Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.65,0:03:21.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, dude, go!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.89,0:03:23.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks, ladies.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.03,0:03:25.03,Default,,0,0,0,,You're beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.69,0:03:26.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Hooray! Hooray!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.63,0:03:29.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Man, what a bunch of suck-ups.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.99,0:03:31.55,Default,,0,0,0,,No yapping, you mutt!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.11,0:03:34.23,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a duel, not a dog show!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.89,0:03:40.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna make my first roll now, Yugi,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.51,0:03:45.31,Default,,0,0,0,,so from here on out you're just gonna have\Nto listen carefully and learn as we go.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.39,0:03:46.86,Default,,0,0,0,,See those markings there?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.05,0:03:48.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Those are called crests.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.73,0:03:50.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Different crests do different things.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.93,0:03:52.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Take that green die, for example.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.41,0:03:56.55,Default,,0,0,0,,That star crest I just\Nrolled is for summoning.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.95,0:03:58.73,Default,,0,0,0,,To be able to summon something,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.81,0:04:01.33,Default,,0,0,0,,at least two out of the three\Ndice that you roll during your
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.41,0:04:04.91,Default,,0,0,0,,turn have to land with the\Nsame type summon crest face-up.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.41,0:04:06.95,Default,,0,0,0,,And if I'm not mistaken,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.27,0:04:09.27,Default,,0,0,0,,it seems I've come up with\Ntwo matching summoning
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.35,0:04:11.81,Default,,0,0,0,,crests on my very first roll of the game.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.15,0:04:14.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, the dimensionalizing\Npart of the process.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.43,0:04:16.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Dimension the dice!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.37,0:04:22.51,Default,,0,0,0,,And there you go! Ryukashin!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.69,0:04:25.23,Default,,0,0,0,,My very first monster is on the board!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.79,0:04:27.73,Default,,0,0,0,,The monsters are inside the dice?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.91,0:04:29.05,Default,,0,0,0,,And that's not all!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.25,0:04:32.07,Default,,0,0,0,,It looks like the dice\Nthemselves are part of the game!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.15,0:04:35.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm glad that you made that point,\Nmy little cheerleader-in-waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.53,0:04:39.65,Default,,0,0,0,,That's one of the key elements to\NDungeon Dice Monsters. For you see,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.89,0:04:44.23,Default,,0,0,0,,once a die unfolds to dimensionalize a\Nmonster, it becomes a dungeon pathway.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.31,0:04:47.59,Default,,0,0,0,,And with enough of this dungeon\Npathway, I can construct a route.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.67,0:04:52.31,Default,,0,0,0,,a route my monsters can use to get\Nto your heart points. Oh, I get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.71,0:04:55.11,Default,,0,0,0,,The way to destroy your\Nopponent's heart points is to get
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.19,0:04:58.27,Default,,0,0,0,,your monsters close enough to\Nattack the hearts directly.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.35,0:05:03.15,Default,,0,0,0,,So, the more dice that I can dimensionalize\Nand turn into Dungeon Path, the better.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.23,0:05:04.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Sounds simple enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.47,0:05:07.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Go ahead, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.07,0:05:09.11,Default,,0,0,0,,It's your turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.91,0:05:11.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Devlin, don't you forget.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.03,0:05:16.03,Default,,0,0,0,,If I win this, then you have to give\Nmy friend Joey his freedom back.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.11,0:05:17.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Right, if you win.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.53,0:05:20.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm counting on you, buddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.23,0:05:22.83,Default,,0,0,0,,If there's anyone that can\Nbeat this guy Devlin, it's you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.91,0:05:24.45,Default,,0,0,0,,No talking, bad dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.57,0:05:26.87,Default,,0,0,0,,We're with you, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.19,0:05:28.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, all the way, buddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.47,0:05:31.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Long live the king of games.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.37,0:05:33.87,Default,,0,0,0,,His reign is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.19,0:05:36.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, this cheat is going down.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.45,0:05:38.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, dice roll.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.09,0:05:43.27,Default,,0,0,0,,The three crests, none of them match.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.63,0:05:46.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, because the level of dice\Nyou threw were way too high.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.95,0:05:50.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, didn't I mention that\Ndifferent dice had different levels?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.81,0:05:53.17,Default,,0,0,0,,This is how it works.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.39,0:05:56.92,Default,,0,0,0,,There are six types of crests\Non the surfaces of these dice.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.01,0:06:03.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Summon, movement, magic, attack,\Ndefense, and trap crests.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.51,0:06:07.41,Default,,0,0,0,,How often each of these crests appears\Non a dice depends on that dice's level.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.49,0:06:11.47,Default,,0,0,0,,The level two dice that I just used\Nhad three summon crests on each,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.55,0:06:13.65,Default,,0,0,0,,so it was easy for me to roll two of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.73,0:06:17.91,Default,,0,0,0,,But the easier a monster is\Nto summon, the weaker he is.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.37,0:06:21.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, now look carefully\Nat your dice, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.27,0:06:25.91,Default,,0,0,0,,They each have only one summon crest.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.53,0:06:31.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Right, and that makes it much more\Ndifficult for you to roll a pair of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.09,0:06:34.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course, had you, it'd have\Nbeen a very strong monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.77,0:06:38.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Still, I'm of the opinion that\Nin the early stages of the game,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.29,0:06:40.27,Default,,0,0,0,,it's better to go for\Na low-level sure thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.35,0:06:45.12,Default,,0,0,0,,After all, the odds of summoning a monster\Nwith high-level dice are slim to none.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.27,0:06:46.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.73,0:06:49.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Almost all the dice I\Npicked were high-level.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.03,0:07:00.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, Yugi, but if all you have are\Nhigh-level dice at your disposal,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.21,0:07:03.65,Default,,0,0,0,,you're going to have a real hard\Ntime summoning any monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.73,0:07:05.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't believe this.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.83,0:07:09.97,Default,,0,0,0,,The game just started, and I'm\Nalready at a huge disadvantage.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.77,0:07:12.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, this ain't fair, Duke.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.87,0:07:15.99,Default,,0,0,0,,You should have told Yugi all the\Nrules before the game started.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.07,0:07:18.89,Default,,0,0,0,,This different dice level\Nstuff changes everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.97,0:07:20.69,Default,,0,0,0,,You should start the game fresh.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.77,0:07:22.73,Default,,0,0,0,,If it were someone else, maybe.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.95,0:07:25.69,Default,,0,0,0,,But not the king of games. He'll be okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.25,0:07:30.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, dice roll!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.63,0:07:34.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.54,0:07:36.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Another two summoning crests.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.23,0:07:40.67,Default,,0,0,0,,My dungeon path will extend, and now\NI'll have two monsters on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.65,0:07:45.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Dimension the dice and unlock Duranto!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.43,0:07:54.21,Default,,0,0,0,,His dungeon path is getting closer\Nand closer to my heart points,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.29,0:07:56.27,Default,,0,0,0,,and I'm not even on the board yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.35,0:07:57.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm coming for you, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.03,0:08:00.63,Default,,0,0,0,,And since I just rolled\Na movement crest too,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.71,0:08:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,I can use it to advance my monster\Neven further along the dungeon pathway.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.01,0:08:09.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, FYI, if you don't want\Nto use a crest you rolled,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.35,0:08:11.97,Default,,0,0,0,,you can save them for\Nlater in your crest pool.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.05,0:08:13.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Now go ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.39,0:08:14.31,Default,,0,0,0,,It's your turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.99,0:08:16.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, dice roll!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.39,0:08:20.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Still no matching crests.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.61,0:08:22.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha-ha, nothing again, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.05,0:08:26.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe you ought to try\Nblowing on them for good luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.35,0:08:27.55,Default,,0,0,0,,My turn now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.97,0:08:29.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, dice roll!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.67,0:08:34.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, would you look at that?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.45,0:08:36.11,Default,,0,0,0,,It's another summoning.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.31,0:08:39.47,Default,,0,0,0,,And look at the surprise inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.31,0:08:41.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Gator dragon.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.93,0:08:45.41,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'll use the movement\Ncrest I rolled to advance him.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.49,0:08:47.75,Default,,0,0,0,,My roll now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.23,0:08:51.45,Default,,0,0,0,,At last, two summoning crests.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.69,0:08:53.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I can play a monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.53,0:08:55.01,Default,,0,0,0,,No, you can't.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.15,0:08:58.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You've rolled two summoning crests,\Nbut their levels aren't the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.57,0:09:00.59,Default,,0,0,0,,It doesn't count. I thought...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.67,0:09:02.01,Default,,0,0,0,,It's my turn again.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.09,0:09:04.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Ooh, level four dice.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.01,0:09:06.95,Default,,0,0,0,,They were too hot for you to handle.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.03,0:09:08.71,Default,,0,0,0,,But let's see how I can do.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.17,0:09:10.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, dice roll!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.57,0:09:15.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, what can I say?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.29,0:09:19.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess Lady Luck has got the hots for\Nold Duke Devlin, like everyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.77,0:09:21.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean, what is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.71,0:09:23.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Four summonings in a row?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.65,0:09:28.69,Default,,0,0,0,,A chest?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.91,0:09:34.31,Default,,0,0,0,,This is an item summoning Yugi, But\Nmore on that a bit later. Now roll.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.51,0:09:39.87,Default,,0,0,0,,No, another miss. You know,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.05,0:09:43.83,Default,,0,0,0,,maybe we should change your title from\Nthe King of Games to the King of Lame.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.91,0:09:47.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean, at this rate, I'll have you\Nbeat even before you're on the board.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.77,0:09:52.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew that you weren't the\Nreal deal, Yugi. Go! Dice roll!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.83,0:09:54.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.77,0:09:55.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Another summoning.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.89,0:09:58.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I'll have a monster\Nright by your heart points.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.75,0:09:59.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Dimension the dice!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.51,0:10:03.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Check it out!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.59,0:10:05.23,Default,,0,0,0,,The 13th Grave!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.01,0:10:12.45,Default,,0,0,0,,That 13th Grave is just three squares\Naway from being able to attack me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.77,0:10:15.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I have to summon a\Nmonster and take him out.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.49,0:10:18.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Otherwise, I'll lose a\Nheart point for sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.17,0:10:19.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on! Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.95,0:10:21.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Our audience is waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.63,0:10:24.73,Default,,0,0,0,,And soon, they're going to see\Nyou for what you really are.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.81,0:10:27.93,Default,,0,0,0,,A loser who could have\Nnever truly beaten Pegasus.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.49,0:10:29.32,Default,,0,0,0,,This is it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.40,0:10:32.32,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter how high the odds\Nare stacked against me,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.41,0:10:35.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I have to believe it's possible\Nto roll two Summon Crests here.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.95,0:10:40.07,Default,,0,0,0,,The same way I believed in the\Nheart of the cards. Go! Dice roll!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.01,0:10:46.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.92,0:10:47.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Not a Summon Crest!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.11,0:10:51.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I got one.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.37,0:10:52.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Now if only...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.45,0:10:59.85,Default,,0,0,0,,There, I rolled two\Nlevel four Summon Crests.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.43,0:11:04.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I can finally summon a monster\Nand defend my heart points.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.93,0:11:06.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Dimension the Dice!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.37,0:11:13.85,Default,,0,0,0,,The Mighty Mage!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.55,0:11:15.49,Default,,0,0,0,,And next,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.63,0:11:19.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll access my Crest Pool Dice and\Nuse a movement crest to move my mage.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.07,0:11:24.15,Default,,0,0,0,,one space forward so he can launch\Nan attack against the 13th grade.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.61,0:11:25.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Lightning step!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.61,0:11:31.33,Default,,0,0,0,,All right! In your face! Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.01,0:11:35.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Knowing this game and all\Nof its rules may have given
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.83,0:11:38.63,Default,,0,0,0,,you the advantage in assembling\Nyour creatures against me,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.71,0:11:41.57,Default,,0,0,0,,but now I have a monster of my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.53,0:11:49.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you see Yugi's last move?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.35,0:11:52.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Incredible!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.43,0:11:54.51,Default,,0,0,0,,He busted out that level four monster like
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.59,0:11:57.18,Default,,0,0,0,,he's played dungeon\Ndice monsters for years!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.09,0:11:59.92,Default,,0,0,0,,You!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.00,0:12:00.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Keep it up, buddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.91,0:12:02.20,Default,,0,0,0,,You're really doing great!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.29,0:12:03.47,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you think, Taya?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.55,0:12:05.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Is Yugi in the clear now?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.09,0:12:06.71,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I don't think so.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.19,0:12:10.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Duke's dungeon path is way\Nmore widespread than Yugi's,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.15,0:12:12.69,Default,,0,0,0,,and he's still got more\Nmonsters out on the board, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.77,0:12:15.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi has a long way to\Ngo to win this game.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.01,0:12:19.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Congratulations on your\Nfirst monster, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.45,0:12:22.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Just four more now, and\Nyou'll have as many as I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.39,0:12:25.27,Default,,0,0,0,,My turn now. Go! Dice roll!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.73,0:12:28.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoops.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.65,0:12:29.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Spoke too soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.75,0:12:30.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Make that five more.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.67,0:12:33.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Dimension the dice!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.91,0:12:39.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I've unlocked the Blast Lizard!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.39,0:12:44.33,Default,,0,0,0,,But don't be fooled by his\Nlow-level status, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.49,0:12:46.19,Default,,0,0,0,,When played in just the right way,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.27,0:12:50.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Last Lizard has a special attack\Nthat packs a surprising punch.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.97,0:12:51.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Special attack?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.27,0:12:55.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Sounds like another rule that Duke\Nconveniently forgot to mention.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.69,0:12:57.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll have to be on my guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.47,0:12:58.67,Default,,0,0,0,,My roll now.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.41,0:13:00.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.49,0:13:01.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Some low-level dice.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.83,0:13:03.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew I had at least a few of these.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.95,0:13:05.87,Default,,0,0,0,,It should be easier to summon now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.95,0:13:07.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, dice roll!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.29,0:13:10.29,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, two crests.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.81,0:13:12.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Dimension the dice!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.15,0:13:19.93,Default,,0,0,0,,The Winged Dragon,\NGuardian of the Fortress.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.23,0:13:23.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Now you have two monsters of\Nmine to contend with, Devlin.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.49,0:13:25.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Not for long, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.25,0:13:27.23,Default,,0,0,0,,It's my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.73,0:13:28.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, dice roll!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.35,0:13:33.15,Default,,0,0,0,,You failed to summon anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.39,0:13:37.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoever said I was trying to\Nsummon a monster on this roll?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.47,0:13:39.30,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.38,0:13:40.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Boy, are you dense.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.73,0:13:44.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember what I said about playing my\Nblast lizard in just the right way?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.75,0:13:47.61,Default,,0,0,0,,So then, you were rolling\Nfor his special attack?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.69,0:13:49.11,Default,,0,0,0,,That's kinda right, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.19,0:13:52.75,Default,,0,0,0,,The Blast Lizard's special attack\Nrequires four Magic Crests.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.83,0:13:57.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I already had two in my Crest pool, so\NI needed to roll two more, which I did.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.37,0:14:01.45,Default,,0,0,0,,So now, I'll use a Movement Crest\Nto position my Blast Lizard.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.59,0:14:05.21,Default,,0,0,0,,And next, use my four Magic\NCrests to have him attack you!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.95,0:14:15.03,Default,,0,0,0,,That's too bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.29,0:14:18.45,Default,,0,0,0,,You worked so hard to summon\Nthat winged dragon, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.29,0:14:20.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Yay!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.20,0:14:21.25,Default,,0,0,0,,We love you, Dookie-Pow!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.35,0:14:23.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't give up.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.59,0:14:24.99,Default,,0,0,0,,You can beat him, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.39,0:14:26.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It's my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.67,0:14:27.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, dice roll!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.49,0:14:32.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Not one summoning crest\Ndied. It's my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.71,0:14:33.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, dice roll!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.79,0:14:37.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, another summoning.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.55,0:14:39.55,Default,,0,0,0,,And with level three dice as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.69,0:14:41.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Dimension the dice!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.87,0:14:45.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Dark assailant!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.39,0:14:52.37,Default,,0,0,0,,And now I'll dip into my crest pool\Nagain and close in on your heart points.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.53,0:14:54.61,Default,,0,0,0,,By using two movement crests,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.69,0:14:59.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I put Blast Lizard and Gator Dragon\Nwithin striking distance of your hearts.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.03,0:15:01.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Go ahead, take your turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.97,0:15:05.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing you roll is going to\Nhelp you get out of this mess.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.83,0:15:09.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean, I don't even think that I'd\Nbe able to find a way to pull it off,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.57,0:15:11.81,Default,,0,0,0,,and I'm the one who invented the game.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.09,0:15:13.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You're its inventor?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.59,0:15:15.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew you were its champion, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.41,0:15:19.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm both, and everyone in the\Nentire world should know it!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.99,0:15:20.82,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.90,0:15:24.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I should be known as the second greatest\Ngame creator in all of the world by now,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.01,0:15:25.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.92,0:15:29.05,Default,,0,0,0,,but I'm not, and it's all\Nbecause of your cheating ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.37,0:15:33.03,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the only way you could have\Nbeaten a great man like Pegasus.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.11,0:15:34.67,Default,,0,0,0,,He has twice the skills you have.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.75,0:15:37.43,Default,,0,0,0,,You ruined my life on that day, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.61,0:15:42.23,Default,,0,0,0,,The defeat that you handed Pegasus\Nchanged everything for me. But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.25,0:15:47.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I dedicated my life to\Ncreating Dungeon Dice Monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.31,0:15:52.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I spent all of my free time perfecting\Nits gameplay and fine-tuning its rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.59,0:15:57.23,Default,,0,0,0,,And when I was finished, it was clear that\NI had created something truly remarkable.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.31,0:16:02.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I decided I had to send it to the only\Nman who could possibly appreciate it,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.61,0:16:03.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Pegasus.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.52,0:16:04.77,Default,,0,0,0,,A couple of days passed,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.87,0:16:06.39,Default,,0,0,0,,but I didn't hear anything from that great
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.47,0:16:10.15,Default,,0,0,0,,game master until I got this crazy e-mail.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.45,0:16:12.39,Default,,0,0,0,,He said he'd read my proposal.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.07,0:16:15.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I couldn't believe my eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.15,0:16:17.81,Default,,0,0,0,,E-mail for Devlin Boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.97,0:16:19.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Email for Devlin Boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.53,0:16:22.09,Default,,0,0,0,,He said he wanted to fly\Nme out on his personal
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.17,0:16:24.95,Default,,0,0,0,,helicopter so that we could\Ndiscuss the game in person.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.03,0:16:25.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.25,0:16:31.31,Default,,0,0,0,,The very next day, I was\Nbrought to Pegasus' island.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.03,0:16:32.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Duelist Kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.27,0:16:34.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I can hardly believe it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.91,0:16:37.17,Default,,0,0,0,,All my hard work was paying off.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.27,0:16:42.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I was going to meet my\Nidol, Maximilian Pegasus.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.67,0:16:48.59,Default,,0,0,0,,When we met, Pegasus immediately challenged\Nme to a game of dungeon dice monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.03,0:16:52.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I expected him to be good,\Nbut he was phenomenal.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.63,0:16:56.67,Default,,0,0,0,,It was his first time playing the\Ngame, and he completely overpowered me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.75,0:16:58.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Me, the guy who created it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.89,0:17:00.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I was amazed with his skills.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.41,0:17:03.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like I win.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.55,0:17:05.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa, you're good.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.67,0:17:11.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, Devlin boy, I must say this Dungeon\NDice Monsters game is really something.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.99,0:17:13.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I thoroughly enjoyed it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.21,0:17:19.47,Default,,0,0,0,,And together, we'll see to it that the\Nwhole world does as well. Partners?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.93,0:17:21.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, I'd be honored, Mr. Pegasus.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.85,0:17:25.11,Default,,0,0,0,,And with that, the deal was sealed.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.09,0:17:31.91,Default,,0,0,0,,He told me we'd draw up the official\Ncontract after he finished hosting a dueling
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.99,0:17:34.25,Default,,0,0,0,,tournament That was about\Nto take place on his
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.33,0:17:37.41,Default,,0,0,0,,island The tournament\Nthat you were headed to,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.57,0:17:42.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi And ever since you beat him there I\Nhaven't been able to contact him at all
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.19,0:17:49.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything that I'd worked for was\Nshattered that day And it's all your
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.89,0:17:55.05,Default,,0,0,0,,fault You don't know what kind of man\NPegasus was at all He was a great man,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.29,0:17:59.83,Default,,0,0,0,,until you came along and broke his\Nspirit with your dirty, cheating ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.13,0:18:02.89,Default,,0,0,0,,And now I'll get my\Nrevenge by breaking you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.97,0:18:14.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Yugi, I'll expose you for what you\Nreally are, a good-for-nothing cheater.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.07,0:18:18.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I've never cheated at anything\Nin my entire life. Please,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.17,0:18:21.59,Default,,0,0,0,,you expect me to believe\Nthat someone like you could
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.67,0:18:24.71,Default,,0,0,0,,defeat a great game master\Nlike Maximillian Pegasus?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.79,0:18:27.77,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't even hold your own\Nin Dungeon Dice Monsters!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.85,0:18:29.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Just listen to me, Devlin! Never!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.57,0:18:34.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Your hero worship of Pegasus has\Ncompletely blinded you to the truth!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.55,0:18:35.38,Default,,0,0,0,,No,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.46,0:18:36.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I can see perfectly,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.43,0:18:40.71,Default,,0,0,0,,and I see a cheater who's about to be\Nretired from Duel Monsters forever!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.79,0:18:42.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Now roll, you fraud!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.67,0:18:45.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I will roll, and I will defeat you!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.93,0:18:48.76,Default,,0,0,0,,There!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.84,0:18:51.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I rolled two level 3 Summon Crests.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.19,0:18:52.96,Default,,0,0,0,,That's another monster for me!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.17,0:18:54.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Dimension the Dice!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.03,0:18:57.61,Default,,0,0,0,,And unlock Thunderball!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.21,0:19:03.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Thunderball.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.91,0:19:08.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Thunderball may be a third level monster,\Nbut his stats really aren't that strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.23,0:19:11.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid he's not going\Nto be a lot of help to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.45,0:19:14.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Unless, that is, Yugi uses\NThunderball's special attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.81,0:19:16.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Too bad he doesn't know how.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.47,0:19:18.75,Default,,0,0,0,,My turn now.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.37,0:19:20.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Go! Dice roll!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.37,0:19:23.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.29,0:19:25.61,Default,,0,0,0,,One attack and two movement crests.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.91,0:19:29.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll advance my blast lizard and\Ngator dragon into attack position.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.81,0:19:32.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Look out, Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.45,0:19:34.86,Default,,0,0,0,,That gator dragon's finally reached Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.95,0:19:36.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi's heart pounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.11,0:19:37.27,Default,,0,0,0,,They're in range.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.75,0:19:40.13,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.33,0:19:43.43,Default,,0,0,0,,My gator dragon is poised\Nto take your heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.97,0:19:50.59,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, Gator Dragon, attack\Nhim with Swamp Fire Blast!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.69,0:19:56.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.97,0:19:59.77,Default,,0,0,0,,He wiped out Yugi's heart\Npoint just like that!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.37,0:20:01.49,Default,,0,0,0,,We love Duke!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.71,0:20:02.99,Default,,0,0,0,,He's so cute!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.21,0:20:04.85,Default,,0,0,0,,When he smiles, he...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.93,0:20:06.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Would y'all shut up?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.05,0:20:08.99,Default,,0,0,0,,My friend's in real trouble here!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.25,0:20:10.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, we're a giant trouble!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.83,0:20:11.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone help me!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.85,0:20:13.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha ha ha ha!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.39,0:20:15.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Now you only have two heart points, Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.87,0:20:16.99,Default,,0,0,0,,But not for long,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.09,0:20:19.09,Default,,0,0,0,,because my monsters are already lined up
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.17,0:20:21.49,Default,,0,0,0,,and ready to take them\Nout in the next round.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.57,0:20:22.49,Default,,0,0,0,,This is bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.81,0:20:25.97,Default,,0,0,0,,The whole world's about\Nto see you lose, Yuge!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.29,0:20:29.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Then you'll be forced to retire\Nfrom dual monsters in shame!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.09,0:20:34.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Pegasus will be avenged, and you'll\Nbe exposed as the sham that you are!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.39,0:20:36.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha ha ha ha!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.35,0:20:38.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Yugi! Ha ha ha!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.29,0:20:39.25,Default,,0,0,0,,What can I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.33,0:20:43.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Duke's got more monsters, more dungeon\Npath and more heart points than me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.71,0:20:46.00,Default,,0,0,0,,And he's in a position to attack again.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.61,0:20:48.31,Default,,0,0,0,,How can I possibly win?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.51,0:20:50.63,Default,,0,0,0,,How can I beat Duke at his own game?
